{
  "concept": "mirror.apply",
  "source": "authored",
  "citation": "docs/mip/0003-own-daemon.md, sections 2 and 9; docs/architecture.md, ownership of truth",
  "why": "The mirror is the core's picture of what a daemon holds: its snapshot, then every event after it, applied in order. The daemon sends whole records, numbered and in order, and nothing from before a snapshot, so every event is applied as it stands and the mirror never has to decide whether one is old news. What it decides is what changed, since that is what the window repaints.\n\nA case is a snapshot, then events, then optionally a second snapshot, which is a reconnect. `panes`, `tabs` and `layouts` are what the mirror holds after all of them, and `changes` is everything the events and the second snapshot reported, in order. Trees render on one line: `columns(p1, p2@0.5)` is p1 beside p2, each at half.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "a snapshot is the whole world, and every pane takes the tab whose tree names it",
      "why": "A daemon's record of a pane does not say which tab holds it; its tab's tree does. Taking it from the trees means the two can never disagree. The tab is announced before its panes and its tree after them, so nothing hears of an arrangement holding a pane it has not been told exists.",
      "given": {
        "snapshot": {
          "tabs": [
            {
              "id": "t1",
              "root": {
                "axis": "columns",
                "ratio": 0.5,
                "first": "p1",
                "second": "p2"
              }
            }
          ],
          "panes": [
            {
              "id": "p1",
              "agentState": "working",
              "cwd": "/src"
            },
            {
              "id": "p2",
              "agentState": "idle",
              "cwd": "/src"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "panes": [
          "p1",
          "p2"
        ],
        "tabs": [
          "t1"
        ],
        "paneTabs": {
          "p1": "t1",
          "p2": "t1"
        },
        "agentStates": {
          "p1": "working",
          "p2": "idle"
        },
        "layouts": {
          "t1": "columns(p1, p2@0.5)"
        },
        "health": "connected",
        "restoring": false,
        "changes": []
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "a pane opened before any tree names it waits until one does",
      "why": "The daemon opens a pane and then changes the tree that places it, and promises no tree names a pane it has not opened. Between the two the pane belongs to no tab, and everything that draws or lists a pane does so by its tab, so it is added when the tree arrives - before that tree is reported.",
      "given": {
        "snapshot": {
          "tabs": [
            {
              "id": "t1",
              "root": "p1"
            }
          ],
          "panes": [
            {
              "id": "p1",
              "agentState": "idle",
              "cwd": "/src"
            }
          ]
        },
        "events": [
          {
            "kind": "paneOpened",
            "id": "p2",
            "agentState": "working",
            "cwd": "/src"
          },
          {
            "kind": "tabChanged",
            "id": "t1",
            "root": {
              "axis": "rows",
              "ratio": 0.5,
              "first": "p1",
              "second": "p2"
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      "expect": {
        "panes": [
          "p1",
          "p2"
        ],
        "tabs": [
          "t1"
        ],
        "paneTabs": {
          "p1": "t1",
          "p2": "t1"
        },
        "agentStates": {
          "p1": "idle",
          "p2": "working"
        },
        "layouts": {
          "t1": "rows(p1, p2@0.5)"
        },
        "health": "connected",
        "restoring": false,
        "changes": [
          "paneAdded:p2",
          "layoutChanged:t1"
        ]
      }
    },
